        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(claws): add portable agent policy settings",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Let Claw manifests select any built-in tool profile registered by OpenClaw.\n- Add portable `alsoAllow`, `deny`, and workspace-only filesystem policy.\n- Add bounded memory-search behavior at the canonical `agent.memory.search` path with explicit cross-conversation consent.\n- Preserve these settings through add, update preview/apply, provenance drift, and export.\n- Classify updates from effective inherited policy, including wildcard profiles, `alsoAllow` grants, and workspace-confinement changes.\n\nThis is the final implementation slice after [#111391](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/111391). It implements the portable-agent-settings addendum in [RFC PR #48](https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/48), building on [Claws RFC #27](https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/27).\n\nHost policy remains authoritative. Claws do not carry custom profile definitions, provider credentials, bindings, local paths, or arbitrary tool/memory configuration. Skill allowlists remain deferred because package refs do not yet establish canonical runtime skill identities.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- Schema accepts registered built-in profiles and rejects unknown profile names.\n- `allow` and `alsoAllow` cannot coexist.\n- `sessions` memory requires `rememberAcrossConversations: true`.\n- Add and export round-trip the canonical `memory.search` shape with no experimental alias.\n- Update preview resolves inherited profiles, filesystem defaults, wildcard capabilities, and memory defaults before classifying escalation or reduction.\n- The downstream ClawHub bridge passes a hosted package into real `claws add --dry-run --json` on this head.\n\n## Validation\n\n- 73 focused schema, export, and capability tests pass.\n- Production core, UI, and extension typechecks pass.\n- Oxlint reports 0 warnings and 0 errors on all changed TypeScript files.\n- `git diff --check` passes.\n",
